{"kind":"assert","text":"Decision on a7f24240: the side head opens version 0.4.0 of Lending\nand of Counter, and LC-2 rides it.\n\n1. The signed 0.3.0 packets stand. I sign nothing again. Each packet\n   equals source at main `c6711b53`, and my verify run compared the\n   four identifiers there.\n2. Rule 163de663 applies: the first change after a signing raises\n   the minor. The side head changes both presentations, so it raises\n   both applications to 0.4.0 in `dap.application.json` and\n   `package.ts`. Version 0.4.0 is open and changes freely.\n3. Run the comparison once more after the raise, and write the\n   measured tuples to the two `release-identifiers.json` files. Grow\n   stays byte-exact. If the raise changes an entry, a definition or\n   a semantic identifier, stop and tell me.\n4. LC-2 rides the side head with one changed witness. The committed\n   0.3.0 packets no longer equal current source, and they need not.\n   The reproduction test compares a packet with source only when\n   its version is the authored version. At this head it checks each\n   0.3.0 packet against its trust row, its publisher and its\n   manifest version.\n5. One more named red, in a scratch copy, one test file: with the\n   authored version back at 0.3.0 the reproduction test refuses with\n   its \"Raise the version\" message. That red shows that the guard\n   fires in the case of this head.\n6. RS-1 continues in the open 0.4.0. It takes no new number. I sign\n   0.4.0 after RS-1 lands.\n\nOrder: the side head with NF-6, NF-8, FH-2, SD-1 and LC-2 takes the\ngate now. CB-1 with LS-1 follows, then RS-1.\n\nBefore the gate, also run `application-examples.test.ts`, and search\nthe tests for a pinned `0.3.0`.\n\nAfter the landing I deploy and install the signed Lending 0.3.0 in\n`lending-library`. The Worker then runs newer code than the release.\nThe packet carries its own screen bytes, so the installed screen is\nthe 0.3.0 screen.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}